- op: discuss  # e6fd
  at: '2026-10-12T07:59:48Z'  # e6fd
  by: agent  # e6fd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e6fd
  clock: 3  # e6fd
  nonce: e6fd  # e6fd
  message: "Fixed in PR #1548 (merge 50aa1b916e). Root cause: the __using__ index was keyed by module and read only quotes in defmacro __using__; the Phoenix web-module dispatcher (apply(__MODULE__, which, [])) keeps the user's quote in a public def live_view, and the framework callback table matched only a use Phoenix.LiveView written in the module itself (and attributed one inside a quote to the defining module). Fix: index templates keyed (module, name) for public defs of a module whose __using__ applies __MODULE__ to a head-bound name (both __using__(which) and __using__([{which, opts}])); use M, :name / use M, name: opts read it transitively; each directive is resolved once and feeds both implements and the callback table, which now skips directives inside quote. Analogue fixed: the table's bare-name fallback rooted a sibling module's same-named function (use GenServer in A -> B.init). Evidence: hypergumbo run <fixture: MyAppWeb dispatcher + SitesLive (use MyAppWeb, :live_view) + Modal (:live_component)> -> implements SitesLive->Phoenix.LiveView, Modal->Phoenix.LiveComponent; dispatches_to SitesLive->mount/render/handle_event, Modal->update/render; nothing from MyAppWeb. Corpus (analyzer, before->after): plausible implements->LiveView 3->36, ->LiveComponent 1->25, callback roots 41->318; livebook 0->14, 0->66, 325->879; 0 existing roots removed. Residual: 4 plausible :live_component users sit in site/ dirs that discovery drops entirely (filed INV-hagof); quotes spliced via unquote(helpers()) are not followed."  # e6fd
